{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>One of the people might have lain.</b> That is, the sole king of his people, who would have thought that he need not ask you or learn your wishes in this matter — for given the king's great excellence, it would surely seem good in your eyes to give him your sister in marriage." "<b>And you would have brought guilt upon us.</b> And thereby you would nearly have brought upon us guilt and punishment. He says 'upon us' because when the leader of the generation is punished, the harm to those who shelter in his shadow increases."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:31:46.196731087Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}